# Use BFQ for SD/MMC storage on joan.
#
# The SD-card install flavour runs the whole rootfs from a microSD card
# (SDR104), not from the phone's UFS. Downstream Android ran cfq against UFS on
# the legacy block layer; the modern blk-mq equivalent for slow, high-latency,
# shallow-queue media is BFQ, which is markedly better than mq-deadline for
# interactive desktop workloads -- session startup on Phosh is dominated by
# small random reads (icon caches, GSettings, fontconfig, shared libraries),
# which is exactly BFQ's case.
#
# UFS/eMMC internal storage keeps the kernel default; only removable MMC is
# retargeted here.
ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="mmcblk[0-9]", ATTR{queue/rotational}=="0", ATTR{queue/scheduler}="bfq"
